{
  "kanda": "yuddha",
  "sarga": 38,
  "title": "Rama decides to stay on Suvela mountain",
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/yuddha/sarga38/yuddhasans38.htm",
  "romanUrl": "https://www.valmikiramayan.net/utf8/yuddha/sarga38/yuddhaitrans38.htm",
  "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy",
  "introduction": [
    "Rama expresses his desire to Vibhishana and Sugreeva to halt on Suvela mountain for that night, and to envision the City of Lanka. Rama along with Lakshmana, Vibhishana, Sugreeva and his army ascend the mountain and witness the beauty of Lanka. They halt on that mountain-resort for the night."
  ],
  "closing": [
    "इत्यार्षे श्रीमद्रामायणे आदिकाव्ये युद्धकाण्डे अष्टात्रिंशः सर्गः",
    "Thus completes 38th Chapter of Yuddha Kanda of the glorious Ramayana of Valmiki, the work of a sage and the oldest epic."
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "6.38.1",
      "label": "6.38.1, 2",
      "numbers": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "devanagari": "स तु कृत्वा सुवेलस्य मतिम् आरोहणम् प्रति |\nलक्ष्मण अनुगतो रामह् सुग्रीवम् इदम् अब्रवीत्\nविभीषणम् च धर्मज्नम् अनुरक्तम् निज़ा चरम् |\nमन्त्रज्नम् च विधिज्नम् च ज़्लक्ष्णया परया गिरा",
      "iast": "sa tu kṛtvā suvelasya matim ārohaṇam prati |\nlakṣmaṇa anugato rāmah sugrīvam idam abravīt\nvibhīṣaṇam ca dharmajnam anuraktam nizā caram |\nmantrajnam ca vidhijnam ca zlakṣṇayā parayā girā",
      "translation": "Rama, who was followed by Lakshmana, having made up his mind to ascend Mount Suvela, spoke in a gentle and prime voice to Sugreeva and to Vibhishana who was the knower of what is right, a demon devoted to him who was experienced in counsel and a knower of prescribed rules (as follows):",
